\frac{x+2}{x^2-4}\times\frac{x-2}{x+3}
Solution: Factorise where possible.
\frac{x+2}{(x-2)(x+2)}\times\frac{x-2}{x+3}
Cancel common factors to get \frac1{x+3}.

\frac{x+1}{x}\div\frac{x^2-1}{x}
Solution: Turn division into multiplication by the fraction’s reciprocal:
\frac{x+1}{x}\times\frac{x}{x^2-1}
Factorise and cancel common factors.
\frac{x+1}{x}\times\frac{x}{(x-1)(x+1)}
=\frac1{x-1}

\frac2{x+1}+\frac3{x-1}
Solution: Find a common denominator.
\frac{2(x-1)}{(x+1)(x-1)}+\frac{3(x+1)}{(x+1)(x-1)}
Simplify the numerator.
\frac{2x-2+3x+3}{(x+1)(x-1)}=\frac{5x+1}{(x+1)(x-1)}

\frac{\frac1{x^2-y^2}+1}{\frac1{x-y}-1}
Solution:
\frac{\frac1{x^2-y^2}+1}{\frac1{x-y}-1}\times\frac{x^2-y^2}{x^2-y^2}
=\frac{1+x^2-y^2}{(x+y)-(x^2-y^2)}
=\frac{1+x^2-y^2}{x+y-x^2+y^2}

